# Who may open "Who sees what" and choose which customers get a new feature.
#
# One email address per line. Everything after a `#` is a note.
#
# Editing this file and pushing it to main applies the list to the running
# backend — a couple of minutes, no other steps. Remove a line and push to
# take the ability away again.
#
# This is deliberately NOT something an account admin can grant themselves.
# A customer's admin administers their own company; if they could also decide
# which companies see unreleased work, "release it to one customer first"
# would stop meaning anything.
#
# An EMPTY list means nobody — the page stays shut. That is the safe direction:
# a deployment that forgets to fill this in must not fall back to "any admin".
